{"tool_name":"tcoffee_sib","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"TCoffee_SIB","home":"http://tcoffee.vital-it.ch/","summary":"A collection of tools for computing, evaluating and manipulating multiple alignments of DNA, RNA, protein sequences and structures. Includes M-Coffee, R-Coffee, Expresso, PSI-Coffee, iRMSD-APDB.","addition_date":"2017-12-06T18:14:55Z","last_update_date":"2020-06-16T10:55:21Z","tool_type":["Suite","Web application"],"collections":["Proteomics","T-Coffee"],"accessibility":"Open access","biotools_curie":"biotools:TCoffee_SIB","cost":"Free of charge","credit":[{"email":"cedric.notredame@europe.com","name":"Cedric Notredame","orcidid":"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-1461-0988","typeEntity":"Person","typeRole":["Primary contact"]}],"documentation":[{"type":["General"],"url":"http://www.tcoffee.org/Projects/tcoffee/"}],"edit_permission":{"authors":["proteomics.bio.tools"],"type":"group"},"function":[{"input":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_2044"}}],"operation":[{"term":"Multiple sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0492"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2403"}],"output":[{"data":{"term":"Sequence alignment","uri":"http://edamontology.org/data_0863"}}]}],"maturity":"Mature","name":"T-Coffee (SIB)","operating_system":["Linux","Mac","Windows"],"owner":"jison","publication":[{"doi":"10.1093/nar/gkr245","metadata":{"abstract":"This article introduces a new interface for T-Coffee, a consistency-based multiple sequence alignment program. This interface provides an easy and intuitive access to the most popular functionality of the package. These include the default T-Coffee mode for protein and nucleic acid sequences, the M-Coffee mode that allows combining the output of any other aligners, and template-based modes of T-Coffee that deliver high accuracy alignments while using structural or homology derived templates. These three available template modes are Expresso for the alignment of protein with a known 3D-Structure, R-Coffee to align RNA sequences with conserved secondary structures and PSI-Coffee to accurately align distantly related sequences using homology extension. The new server benefits from recent improvements of the T-Coffee algorithm and can align up to 150 sequences as long as 10000 residues and is available from both http://www.tcoffee.org and its main mirror http://tcoffee.crg.cat. \u00a9 2011 The Author(s).","authors":[{"name":"Chang J.-M."},{"name":"Di Tommaso P."},{"name":"Montanyola A."},{"name":"Moretti S."},{"name":"Notredame C."},{"name":"Orobitg M."},{"name":"Taly J.-F."},{"name":"Xenarios I."}],"citationCount":605,"date":"2011-07-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nucleic Acids Research","title":"T-Coffee: A web server for the multiple sequence alignment of protein and RNA sequences using structural information and homology extension"},"pmcid":"PMC3125728","pmid":"21558174","type":["Primary"]}],"topic":[{"term":"Genomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0622"},{"term":"Proteomics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0121"},{"term":"Sequence analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0080"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"T-Coffee (SIB)","home":"https://bio.tools/TCoffee_SIB","summary":"A collection of tools for computing, evaluating and manipulating multiple alignments of DNA, RNA, protein sequences and structures. Includes M-Coffee, R-Coffee, Expresso, PSI-Coffee, iRMSD-APDB.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:tcoffee_sib/suite/tcoffee.vital-it.ch","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"documentation":{"general":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":622,"citations":[{"count":4,"year":"2011"},{"count":15,"year":"2026"},{"count":24,"year":"2012"},{"count":34,"year":"2014"